  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "AND for critical hosts",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand: a composite's function is the OR over its host's minimal unsatisfiable sets of the AND of their atoms' bits (lemma M), so it is AND whenever every replaced line is critical; every line of every Kasteleyn knot sphere is critical (lemma H: every set S of lines touches at least |S| + 2 faces, then Hall); growth by good critical atoms keeps criticality (lemma G). So AND is the only function over every host built from knot spheres and class-forced lattice tori. Checked: 16 spheres, and the AND exactly over three non-octahedral hosts.",
